in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/pact

# @mirror/spec/property — the substrate-decl'd shape of a spec-native
# `property <name> { verifies { <expr> } domain @<T> samples <n>
# defer? <msg> }` block.
#
# Companion to shards/mirror/spec.mirror (which declares the @mirror/spec
# prism + top-level `project NAME { ... }` grammar). Registers the
# spec-body `property` block as a first-class grammar construct so
# mirror.spec files can carry spec-native property declarations
# consumed by the rust/src/liquid.rs runtime (per Mara 2026-07-19
# canonical spec docs/specs/2026-07-19-mirror-spec-is-the-fixpoint-
# liquid-is-the-runtime.md §3.3 Step 1).
#
# The bootstrap's keyword harvester (bootstrap/src/grammar.rs::
# merge_keyword_sources + companion_keyword_sources) reads `<op>
# <keyword>` 2-word lines inside a `grammar { ... }` block to build
# the tokenizer's keyword table; this file is the substrate-altitude
# declaration of those bindings for the spec-native property shape.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - Alex 2026-07-19 in-transcript verbatim (ratification):
#     "The mirror.spec is already the fixpoint. This means you can
#      shape the geometry of the project by writing the properties
#      into the spec. [...] the properties [...] want to be wired
#      into liquid.rs into the matrix.rs and become basically the
#      RUNTIME that parses the mirror.spec and infers and verifies
#      the shape of the geometry."
#
# - Canonical spec: docs/specs/2026-07-19-mirror-spec-is-the-fixpoint-
#   liquid-is-the-runtime.md (Mara 2026-07-19; §2.5 Q5 answer + §3.3
#   registration plan + §3.1 property carrier syntax).
#
# - Math foundation: docs/math/the-tower/recognition-mirror-spec-is-
#   the-fixpoint-and-liquid-is-the-runtime.md (Mara 2026-07-19; §10
#   formal property carrier notation + §2 fixpoint theorem + §3 `---`
#   separator as boundary operator).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# The `property` vocabulary was already substrate-decl'd across 9+
# LANDED property shards under shards/epistemologic/property/*:
#
#   cold_compile_within_tolerance    (Tick 43; 2026-06-20)
#   dark_count_monotone              (Tick 41; 2026-06-19)
#   docblock_grounded                (Trio slot 1; 2026-07-06)
#   docblock_coherent                (Trio slot 2; 2026-07-06)
#   docblock_no_extraction_pattern   (Trio slot 3; 2026-07-06)
#   restart_intensity_well_formed    (2026-07-03)
#   verdict_is_content_addressed     (N1 Tick 1; 2026-07-12)
#   ouroboros_monotone               (Arc-1 Tick 1.5 Landing 7; 2026-07-15)
#   tool_species_stagefreight_witnessed  (2026-07-18)
#
# All follow the docblock + species-decl + `<name>(args) -> verdict
# { \ }` obligation-blocked action shape. This companion extends the
# vocabulary to spec-body altitude — where a project's mirror.spec
# names the properties that project's settlement must satisfy.
#
# The vocabulary is NOT new. What's new is admitting it inside a
# spec-body block. The two altitudes coexist:
#
#   shards/epistemologic/property/<name>.mirror    — substrate-decl'd
#                                                    at family altitude;
#                                                    declares WHAT the
#                                                    property means.
#   mirror.spec `property <name> { ... }` block    — project-declared
#                                                    at spec altitude;
#                                                    declares that THIS
#                                                    project's settlement
#                                                    must satisfy the
#                                                    named property (or
#                                                    a spec-local
#                                                    predicate defined
#                                                    inline).
#
# === Relation to bilateral (Q2 answer — BOTH coexisting) ===
#
# Per Mara 2026-07-19 canonical spec §2.2: bilateral is the degenerate
# case of property (single sentinel-containment `verifies` expression);
# property is the general form. The 30 landed bilateral declarations
# at shards/**/*.mirror continue to work unchanged; their
# `bilateral <name> { sentinel "..." arity N require <ref>* }` shape
# parses under shards/epistemologic/pact/keywords.mirror (LANDED
# 2026-07-16) at shard-body altitude. This property companion carrier
# admits the general property form at spec-body altitude.
#
# Coexistence is permanent. The choice between bilateral (shard-body,
# byte-substring-check) and property (spec-body, algebraic/parametric/
# defer) is ergonomic, not semantic — both dispatch through the same
# generic dispatch(addr, args) -> Verdict (per math root §5 three-
# dispatcher collapse theorem).
#
# === Companion-source registration (Reed post-landing tick) ===
#
# Per canonical spec §3.3 Step 2: Reed adds ONE line to
# bootstrap/src/grammar.rs::companion_keyword_sources's match arm for
# "shards/mirror/spec.mirror":
#
#   "shards/mirror/spec.mirror" => &[
#       "shards/mirror/spec/keywords.mirror",
#       "shards/mirror/spec/property.mirror",   // NEW
#   ],
#
# The extension is additive per merge_keyword_sources's missing-file-
# is-not-fatal semantics (bootstrap/src/grammar.rs line 244); removing
# the companion regresses cleanly. Same precedent as shards/mirror/
# spec/keywords.mirror (2026-06-09) and shards/song/keywords.mirror
# (2026-07-13, Path B).
#
# === Kinds chosen so the tokenizer's existing per-kind path produces
# === the right shape:
#
#   focus    — opens a recursively-scanned brace block. Top-level
#              `property NAME { ... }` uses this so the four inner
#              directives (verifies / domain / samples / defer) parse
#              as child AST nodes of the property declaration.
#              `verifies { <expr> }` itself opens a nested brace block
#              (the obligation body); focus-kind admits the recursive
#              descent.
#              Same precedent as `focus project` / `focus target` /
#              `focus cli` in shards/mirror/spec/keywords.mirror and
#              `focus bilateral` in shards/epistemologic/pact/
#              keywords.mirror.
#
#   project  — single-line directive that consumes one identifier /
#              string-literal / integer / ref as its `name` field, no
#              brace block. Used for `domain @<Type>` /
#              `samples <n>` / `defer <msg>`.
#              Same precedent as `project sentinel` / `project arity` /
#              `project require` in shards/epistemologic/pact/
#              keywords.mirror.
#
# These bindings are the dispatch surface the runtime reads;
# property_decl (below) is the substrate's semantic surface. Both
# coexist by design — the keyword bindings are the grammar-loader's
# parse surface; the shard-decl is the substrate's typed carrier the
# runtime consumes.

grammar @mirror/spec/property {
  # === property block (recursively scanned body) ===
  #
  # Top-level `property <name> { ... }` block declaring a spec-native
  # property whose runtime obligation dispatches to prismqueer::liquid::
  # pillar primitives (per canonical spec §2.3 Q3 answer).
  #
  # Scope: valid inside a top-level `project NAME { ... }` block only;
  # invalid at file top-level. Enforced by property_decl_placement_
  # coherent bilateral below.
  focus property

  # === property fields ===
  #
  # `verifies { <expression-tree> }` — the obligation body. An
  # expression tree in the bounded sub-Turing fragment (per
  # docs/math/liquid-types/README.md §1.1 Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala 2008
  # decidability grounding). Evaluates to a boolean (Pass/Fail) or a
  # PropertyVerdict value (Pass / Fail / Partial).
  # `focus` kind so the `{ ... }` body parses as child AST nodes of
  # the property declaration; the expression-tree grammar itself is
  # sketched at canonical spec §3.2 (v0.1 minimum: boolean literals +
  # composition, equality on Metric-valued expressions, sentinel-
  # containment, method calls on domain-typed values, universally-
  # quantified sub-loops, pillar-primitive direct calls).
  focus verifies

  # `domain @<Type>` — the domain of universally-quantified variables
  # in the verifies expression. `@TestBundle`, `@Signature`, `@Byte`,
  # `@Source`, `@Perm3`, etc. Domains are substrate-decl'd types; the
  # domain-ref resolves to the type's Arbitrary witness (per
  # prism/prismqueer/src/liquid.rs::Sample; substrate-decl'd counterpart
  # forward-promised per canonical spec Q-Mara-E).
  project domain

  # `samples <n>` — the number of sampled instances the runtime
  # quantifies over. Passed to pillar::forall(n, f). Bounded above by
  # a substrate-decl'd budget (per @resource-budget/* forward-promise).
  # Integer literal; positive; bounded above by budget-decl'd max.
  project samples

  # `defer <message>` — optional. Marks the property as operationally-
  # deferred: runtime issues Partial(defer, message) verdicts until
  # the substrate can discharge. Per Reed's `defer()`-mode pattern in
  # prism/prismqueer/tests/red_trust_chain_liquid_void.rs (`560ea67`)
  # + red_narcissus_battery_five_op_collapse.rs (`60df742`).
  # String literal payload; explanatory message for the deferral.
  project defer
}

# === typed carrier: property_decl ===
#
# The substrate-decl'd carrier for a parsed `property <name> { ... }`
# block. Extracted by rust/src/liquid.rs::extract_properties (Reed
# post-landing per canonical spec §8.2 Tick M1) from mirror.spec via
# the standard bootstrap grammar path (line-scan header parsing,
# body-line consumption, brace-tracking — mirrors bootstrap/src/apply_h.
# rs::extract_bilaterals line 209 pattern).
#
# Fields per canonical spec §3.1:
#
#   name                     — identifier; unique across spec + shard corpus
#   verifies_expression_tree — the parsed verifies block (bounded
#                              sub-Turing fragment per §3.2)
#   domain_type_witness      — ref to substrate-decl'd type with
#                              Arbitrary witness
#   samples_count            — positive integer; bounded by
#                              @resource-budget/*
#   defer_annotation         — option(str); Some(msg) marks property as
#                              deferred with the given message
#
# Consumer: rust/src/liquid.rs::dispatch_property (Reed post-landing
# per canonical spec §8.3 Tick M2) matches the verifies expression
# shape to a pillar primitive (dispatch table at math root §4.2), then
# invokes primitive with domain-sampled args.
property_decl(
  name: identifier,
  verifies_expression_tree: expression_tree,
  domain_type_witness: ref,
  samples_count: nat,
  defer_annotation: option(str)
) -> property_decl { \ }

# === well-formedness bilateral ===
#
# `property_decl_well_formed` — the base bilateral gating admissibility
# of a parsed property_decl. Sentinel byte-string encodes the four
# admissibility criteria (name-unique + verifies-non-empty + domain-
# resolvable + samples-positive) as a single content-addressed witness.
#
# Base bilateral (arity 1); dispatched by apply_h::act (or its rust/
# successor per canonical spec §5.2) via the standard reflective
# corpus-lookup path (bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs::load_bilateral_corpus
# + discharge). No `require` clauses — the four criteria are checked
# by the sentinel-containment path on the property_decl's oid.
bilateral property_decl_well_formed {
  sentinel "property-decl=name-unique-verifies-nonempty-domain-resolvable-samples-positive"
  arity 1
}
property_decl_well_formed(p: property_decl) -> verdict { \ }

# === scope bilateral ===
#
# `property_decl_placement_coherent` — a base bilateral gating the
# STRUCTURAL scope invariant: a `property <name> { ... }` block is
# valid inside a top-level `project NAME { ... }` block only; invalid
# at .spec file top-level or nested inside a `target NAME { ... }`
# block.
#
# Rationale: properties are project-level concerns per canonical spec
# §2.1 Q1 answer (spec-native primary, shard-decl secondary). Nesting
# discipline mirrors `focus cli` placement (target-body only) and
# `focus tools` forward-promise placement (project-body only).
#
# Sentinel byte-string encodes the placement invariant as a single
# content-addressed witness; dispatched via the standard reflective
# corpus path.
bilateral property_decl_placement_coherent {
  sentinel "property-decl=project-body-scoped-not-target-body-not-file-top"
  arity 1
}
property_decl_placement_coherent(p: property_decl) -> verdict { \ }

# === composed admissibility bilateral ===
#
# `property_decl_admissible` — the composed bilateral gating full
# admissibility of a parsed property_decl. AND-conjuncts:
#
#   property_decl_well_formed(p)         — four-criterion admissibility
#   property_decl_placement_coherent(p)  — scope invariant
#
# Per canonical spec §5.2 discharge pseudocode: composed bilaterals
# AND-conjunct sub-bilaterals via `require`; return Fail on first
# non-Pass. Same pattern as shards/peer/persistence.mirror's
# `home_witnessing` (5-conjunct composed) and shards/kintsugi/roomba.
# mirror's `walk_witnessing` (5-conjunct composed).
#
# Consumer: mirror.spec dispatcher (rust/src/liquid.rs::extract_
# properties) invokes property_decl_admissible on every parsed
# property_decl BEFORE runtime dispatch to pillar; ill-formed or
# ill-placed declarations fail admissibility and emit a diagnostic
# instead of dispatching a runtime discharge.
bilateral property_decl_admissible {
  sentinel "property-decl=well-formed-and-placement-coherent"
  arity 1
  require property_decl_well_formed
  require property_decl_placement_coherent
}
property_decl_admissible(p: property_decl) -> verdict { \ }

out @mirror/spec/property
out property
out verifies
out domain
out samples
out defer
out property_decl
out property_decl_well_formed
out property_decl_placement_coherent
out property_decl_admissible
